  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business Angel Network training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project builds on earlier Private Sector Development (PSD) projects PCB23PS02 and PCB25PS01, which addressed the limited access to finance faced by early-stage (micro-,) small- and medium-sized enterprises ((M)SMEs) and young entrepreneurs in the Palestinian Territories by establishing a Business Angel Network (BAN). With the first group of angel investors successfully onboarded, the next step is to strengthen their capacity through tailored training.The project provides a structured training programme for BAN members and, where relevant, the BAN management team. It begins with a needs assessment carried out by BeyondCapital in close consultation with FLOW Accelerator, ensuring that the curriculum reflects the network&#x2019;s specific requirements. Training topics for angels include startup evaluation, risk assessment, due diligence, deal structuring, exit strategies, and portfolio management, as well as principles of impact investing, responsible business conduct and investment ethics. BAN management may receive additional training in governance, member relations, and dealroom facilitation.By equipping both investors and management with practical skills, the project transforms the BAN into a credible, professional network that enables entrepreneurs in the Palestinian Territories to access early-stage finance and grow sustainably.</narrative>
  </description>
